# kept by Samwise Gamgee, on the back of a Bag End shopping list
# timestamps are guesses: no sun, no stars, no sense in it
# Shire calendar: every month has 30 days

3019-02-29 dusk    left the Emyn Muil. rope retrieved (it came down on its own; elf-rope).
3019-02-29 dusk    guide says the marshes are the only way. guide also says "no hurry".
3019-03-01 03:00   guide went off to eat something. did not ask what.
3019-03-01 dawn    fog. mud. more mud. Mr Frodo quiet.
3019-03-01 noon    guide found a path. says it has been here before. believes him, sadly.
3019-03-01 dusk    lights. do not follow them. we did not follow them.
3019-03-01 22:00   Mr Frodo said he could see faces. told him not to. he kept looking.
3019-03-02 00:30   WARN  I looked. once. I am not writing down what I saw.
3019-03-02 02:10   Mr Frodo fell in, half-way. out now. dry-ish. nobody mention it.
3019-03-02 05:00   lights out. guide in a better mood; won't say why.
3019-03-02 11:40   CRIT  something big with wings went over, west. all three flat in the reeds.
3019-03-02 11:41   guide shaking, says "wraiths on wings". did not ask how he knows.
3019-03-02 17:00   ground getting harder. nothing growing. worse, somehow.
3019-03-02 19:30   out of the marshes. the plain ahead is all slag and stones.
3019-03-02 19:31   INFO  guide was right the whole way across. noted, for fairness.
3019-03-02 19:32   still don't trust him.
